otto-agent-protocol ports the provider-runtime design of T3 Code
(https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code — the clone studied was at commit
cefb544af3c98224874419198c0359b652ca3c94). Ported parts: the provider runtime
event model and entities, the ACP session lifecycle and update mapping, the
Claude Agent SDK transport and decision mapping (ClaudeAdapterV2), the Codex
app-server lifecycle, item and approval mapping (CodexAdapterV2), the Grok
ACP launch flavour, the 50 ms streaming coalescing, the replay/snapshot
limits and the restart reconciliation. Later fixes ported from T3 Code
(main at 3ffd38ef7, behaviour only): #34597 (a cut-off reply reads
interrupted), #34183 (an interrupted Claude tool call is stopped, not
failed), #34912 (Stop on a turn that is still starting), #34564 (a model
picked with a steer switches the running turn), #34822 (a resumed Claude
waits for its MCP servers), #34762 (a passing resume refusal keeps the
conversation), #34505 (jobs that left the CLI's process group are stopped),
#34771 (Codex MCP startup failures as notices), #34782 (a failed ACP config
write is retried), #33604 (a resumed ACP message keeps its text), #34867
(an ACP choice and its `__other` field are one question) and the open
#31370 (Claude's context meter uses the window Claude enforces). Its
